  "arrangerNotes": "9/8 time (eighth = 0.5 beat). Verse 1, vocal line, verified against the Wikisource LilyPond transcription of the 1864/65 Pond first edition (pages 2–3); the piano part is left out. Simplifications: (1) the chromatic E♮ neighbour note in 'wake unto me', 'heard in the day' and 'life's busy throng' (written F–E♮–F) is played as the scale tone 1 (E♭ in the original key), since tongue drums have no chromatic notes; (2) the small grace note in the final 'awake unto me' is left out. Source correction: in bar 21 the Wikisource transcription writes the first note an octave too high (C6); the original 1865 scan on Wikimedia Commons (page 3) shows C5, matching bar 19, so we use that. D drum: as written (range low 7 to high 2), D minLayout 13. C drum: the C drum has no high 2, so the line 'List while I woo thee with soft melody' (score events 48–57) is played one octave lower; C minLayout 11. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
}
